> Okay, so I can see the image trace points, so I think I've got an image trace, but when I try to change its color, the whole square containing the points gets colored.
**assistant**:
> It sounds like you may be trying to apply color to the entire object, which is likely due to the way you’re selecting or filling the shapes after tracing. Here’s how to successfully change colors of specific components after you’ve traced the image:
> 
> 1. **Expand the Image Trace:**
>    - Make sure your Image Trace is expanded. Select the traced image and go to `Object > Image Trace > Expand`. This converts the tracing into individual vector paths.
> 
> 2. **Ungroup the Traced Elements:**
>    - After expanding, the entire image may still be grouped as one object. To edit individual parts, you’ll want to ungroup them. 
>    - With the traced image selected, go to `Object > Ungroup` (or right-click and choose "Ungroup").
>    - You may need to repeat this step if there are still parts grouped together.
> 
> 3. **Select Specific Components:**
>    - Once ungrouped, you can select individual shapes or paths within your image. Use the Selection Tool (V) to click on the part you want to change.
>    - If you want to select multiple parts, hold down the Shift key while clicking on each one.
> 
> 4. **Change the Color:**
>    - With the desired shapes selected, go to the Color panel (Window > Color) or use the Fill box in the toolbar.
>    - You can choose a new color either by selecting from the color wheel, entering values, or using the Eyedropper Tool (I) to sample colors from other artwork.
> 
> 5. **Adjust Further (if needed):**
>    - If you want to change more colors or want finer control, you can use the `Recolor Artwork` feature:
>      - Select all the paths you want to change.
>      - Go to `Edit > Edit Colors > Recolor Artwork`, and adjust colors using the settings there.
> 
> 6. **Use Layers (if needed):**
>    - If you want to maintain some organization, you can use layers (Window > Layers) to manage and lock certain elements while working on others.
> 
> After following these steps, you should be able to change the colors of individual components of your traced image without affecting the entire square containing the points. Let me know if you need further assistance!
